      "anchor_end": 2015,
      "anchor_kind": "reviewed_current_document_passage",
      "anchor_start": 1797,
      "anchor_text": "Important factors that could cause actual results to differ materially include: global economic and political conditions; NVIDIA’s reliance on third parties to manufacture, assemble, package and test NVIDIA’s products;",
      "case_key": "DELL",
      "evidence_item_digest": "9b05477354785b107d379ae69551304da3d09bcd5ceb56979d4fe621589a26a5",
      "review_status": "reviewed_exact_source_surface",
      "source_record_id": "8K_EARNINGS::NVDA::000104581026000051::Q1FY27PRHTM::BLOCK_0003::CHUNK_0001",
      "source_text_digest": "ffdbfdf055973e3a9c6f3f976a3374e4953cf17906136dc28aba108dfcb74cec",
      "target_id": "8K_EARNINGS::NVDA::000104581026000051::Q1FY27PRHTM::BLOCK_0003::CHUNK_0001_CLAIM_EBFEA572"
    },
    {
      "anchor_digest": "165e9226cbb1f16a3e2f35dd1c5d7cd383d28f9e4b6cc0278df865b4e69bed5b",
      "anchor_end": 839,
      "anchor_kind": "reviewed_current_document_passage",
      "anchor_start": 594,
      "anchor_text": "The memory uncertainty is driving customers to proactively secure access to infrastructure across both traditional and AI workloads over longer periods of time. We also continued to execute the pricing and margin discipline we established in Q4.",
      "case_key": "DELL",
      "evidence_item_digest": "e56d04955adef83b83bbbfda0bb36ed3967f869d34f9473849777a52d40f5305",
      "review_status": "reviewed_exact_source_surface",
      "source_record_id": "CURRENT_DOC::DELL::EARNINGS_CALL_TRANSCRIPT::0D030B0885B1F6EEB005::PAGE_003",
      "source_text_digest": "13e051cfba20ea450890394b06073b30c8b107fcaa3c4a7ea7b5fdaaaaec131a",
      "target_id": "CURRENT_DOC::DELL::EARNINGS_CALL_TRANSCRIPT::0D030B0885B1F6EEB005::PAGE_003::CLAIM::13E051CFBA20"
    },
    {
      "anchor_digest": "410c5a97c13df378047d5f5572ecf5c1bf3dad1831f8589c8f38cb46493b7f02",
      "anchor_end": 1080,
      "anchor_kind": "reviewed_current_document_passage",
      "anchor_start": 557,
      "anchor_text": "In Q1, we booked $24.4 billion in AI orders and recognized $16.1 billion of AI server revenue. We exited the quarter with a record $51.3 billion of AI backlog, and our pipeline continued to grow sequentially and remains multiples of our backlog, even after converting $24.4 billion into orders. Demand continues to exceed supply with memory as the primary constraint and we expect to exit the year with meaningful backlog. Our customer count surpassed 5,000 with growth across neocloud, sovereigns and enterprise customers.",
      "case_key": "DELL",
      "evidence_item_digest": "a35dc0a2d0492238478869c5af6f41d7114d96ef2dba0502291b0b96c031e2b1",
      "review_status": "reviewed_exact_source_surface",
      "source_record_id": "CURRENT_DOC::DELL::EARNINGS_CALL_TRANSCRIPT::0D030B0885B1F6EEB005::PAGE_003",
      "source_text_digest": "9ba6ea00e4ed9deb198330cc02cfdd78868229f6ccb582ce996d604f2d413a60",
      "target_id": "CURRENT_DOC::DELL::EARNINGS_CALL_TRANSCRIPT::0D030B0885B1F6EEB005::PAGE_003::CLAIM::9BA6EA00E4ED"
    },
    {
      "anchor_digest": "b9189ccb5a6bdc9bb7bdbf6ed2f1efcc785a7a24cf1d541ba543d4d4c6724bb1",
      "anchor_end": 645,
      "anchor_kind": "reviewed_current_document_passage",
      "anchor_start": 553,
      "anchor_text": "AI server profitability was in line with our mid- single-digit operating income rate target.",
      "case_key": "DELL",
      "evidence_item_digest": "b8880e2b4c9fe482e2721a00b636ed8cf689f9b0a3ba67a661085a1eacfd11e1",
      "review_status": "reviewed_exact_source_surface",
      "source_record_id": "CURRENT_DOC::DELL::EARNINGS_CALL_TRANSCRIPT::0D030B0885B1F6EEB005::PAGE_004",
      "source_text_digest": "106e3ced4229ac07ef31aeffd5931e91a854b64021ce9f7b29f77a2def499ccb",
      "target_id": "CURRENT_DOC::DELL::EARNINGS_CALL_TRANSCRIPT::0D030B0885B1F6EEB005::PAGE_004::CLAIM::106E3CED4229"
    },
    {
      "anchor_digest": "b69456c4a4d4a59ae6f4b324d933a05f9c5b1a9d1ff87180598a5936ffe83d35",
      "anchor_end": 599,
      "anchor_kind": "structured_claim_text",
      "anchor_start": 284,
      "anchor_text": "Given the scale of the AI opportunities, the varying stages of customer readiness, and the frequency of component part updates or transitions, there is inherent non-linearity in the timing of demand and subsequent shipments for our AI-optimized server offerings, which continues to drive variability in our revenue.",
      "case_key": "DELL",
      "evidence_item_digest": "bcb7ba6a7ca507f8f3cecf44a5b77164c82852518a62768739e14f7fc52b4183",
      "review_status": "reviewed_exact_source_surface",
      "source_record_id": "DELL_2026_10Q_ITEM2_BLOCK_0004_CHUNK_0001",
